Netflix VMAF
============

This directory redistributes licensing materials for the official Netflix VMAF
project (https://github.com/Netflix/vmaf), used by PixVQA for optional CPU VMAF
evaluation via libvmaf commit 74f930d17de8c58e7c2ce55e2b897b0030ebd8ef.
That commit is not a tagged release. The previous tagged revision remains
v3.2.1.

Pinned upstream revision
------------------------

- Repository: https://github.com/Netflix/vmaf
- Commit: 74f930d17de8c58e7c2ce55e2b897b0030ebd8ef
- Previous tag: v3.2.1
- Previous commit: f85a853692a8c730d0270cd733c8bb30b5b93b7c
- Picture conversion: zimg 3.0.6, commit f819b14e8f39d1282400b0d9543e8ef73c1b2bbd
  (https://github.com/sekrit-twc/zimg). zimg is linked, not vendored as source.

Vendored model JSON assets
--------------------------

The eight VMAF v1.0.16 model JSON files under `model/` are exact byte copies
of the corresponding files from v3.2.1. The eight HDR VMAF v1.1.8 files under
`model/hdr_vmaf_v1.1.8/` and `model/hdr_vmaf_v1.1.8_hfr/` are exact byte copies
from commit 74f930d. See `model/README.md` and `reports/VMAF_MODEL_CHECKSUMS.md`.

